  "notes": "{擦|す}り{切|き}れる describes things wearing thin or through from friction or repeated use. A compound verb from {擦|す}る (to rub) + {切|き}れる (to break/snap).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {擦|す}り{切|き}る (transitive — to wear something out)\n- Pattern: 〜が{擦|す}り{切|き}れる\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {擦|す}り{切|き}れている: is worn out (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {靴下|くつした}が{擦|す}り{切|き}れる: socks wear out\n- ズボンの{膝|ひざ}が{擦|す}り{切|き}れる: pants knees wear through\n- {本|ほん}の{背表紙|せびょうし}が{擦|す}り{切|き}れる: book spine wears out\n- ロープが{擦|す}り{切|き}れる: rope frays through\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {破|やぶ}れる: to tear, to rip\n- {傷|いた}む: to become damaged\n- {古|ふる}びる: to become old/worn looking",
